<title>DENMARK: Danish July unemployment rises to 9.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Danish July unemployment rises to 9.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's seasonally adjusted unemployment was 9.1 pct of the workforce in July, up from 8.7 percent in June, the National Statistics Office said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>				July 1996  June 1996  July 1995</p>
<p>    Unemployment rate     9.1 pct   8.7 pct    10.6 pct</p>
<p>    Total unemployed     254,900    244,400    297,300</p>
<p>All above figures seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>NOTE - Seven economists polled by Reuters had on average forecast July unemployment of 9.0 percent.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom, 45-33-969650.</p>
</text>
